# Mason Bricks — Authoring Guide

All mason bricks live under `mason_templates/bricks/<brick_name>/`. After **any** edit to a brick you must recompile it — the generated `lib/src/templates/<brick_name>_bundle.dart` is what the CLI actually uses at runtime.

## Brick Structure

```
mason_templates/bricks/<brick_name>/
  brick.yaml          # Name, version, var declarations
  __brick__/          # Template files — Mustache-interpolated at generation time
  README.md           # Optional
  CHANGELOG.md        # Optional
```

## Mustache Syntax Cheatsheet

| Syntax | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `{{variable}}` | Interpolate a string variable |
| `{{#flag}}...{{/flag}}` | Render only when `flag` is `true` |
| `{{^flag}}...{{/flag}}` | Render only when `flag` is `false` |
| `{{> partial.dart }}` | Include a partial template (e.g., licence header) |
| `{{#flag}}dirname{{/flag}}` | **Directory name** is conditional on `flag` |

Variable names used in this project are defined in `lib/src/commands/create_command.dart` (the vars dict passed to mason). Always check that file before adding new template variables.

## Conditional File & Directory Inclusion

To include a file only when a flag is enabled, place it inside a directory whose name uses the flag syntax:

```
__brick__/{{#enable_feature_counter}}feature_counter{{/enable_feature_counter}}/
```

For conditional content within a file, wrap sections with `{{#flag}}...{{/flag}}`.

## Conditional Imports Pattern

Place conditional imports at the top of a file in flag blocks:

```dart
{{#enable_login}}
import '../../feature_login/blocs/login_bloc.dart';
{{/enable_login}}
```

## Partials

The `licence.dart` partial is available everywhere:

```dart
{{> licence.dart }}
```

## The `rx_bloc_base` Brick

This is the **base brick** — it holds the always-present scaffold. Feature-specific files live in **separate bricks** (e.g., `feature_login`, `lib_auth`) and are merged in by `BundleGenerator`. Do not add feature-specific files directly to `rx_bloc_base` unless they are always needed.

### Key directories in `rx_bloc_base/__brick__/`

| Path | Notes |
|---|---|
| `lib/base/` | Always-present application base classes |
| `lib/feature_splash/` | Always included |
| `lib/feature_home/` | Always included |
| `lib/feature_dashboard/` | Always included |
| `lib/lib_router/` | Added by `lib_router` brick (always merged) |
| `.cursor/rules/` | Cursor rules included in generated projects |
| `.agents/skills/` | Agent skills included in generated projects |
| `.vscode/` | VS Code settings for generated projects |

## Compiling Bricks

After editing any brick, regenerate its bundle dart file:

```sh
# Compile a single brick
dart run mason_cli:mason bundle -t dart -o lib/src/templates/ mason_templates/bricks/<brick_name>

# Compile all bricks
bin/compile_bundles.sh
```

The compiled bundle is a single Dart file with all brick content base64-encoded. **Never edit it manually.**

## Adding a Brick to the CLI

After compiling, wire it up in the Dart source:

1. Import the bundle in `lib/src/models/bundle_generator.dart`
2. Add a field `final _myBundle = myBrickBundle;`
3. Add conditional logic: `if (arguments.myFeatureEnabled) { _bundle.files.addAll(_myBundle.files); }`
4. Add the `create_mason_bundle my_brick` line to `bin/compile_bundles.sh`

## Testing Brick Output

```sh
# Generate a full project and inspect
bin/generate_test_project.sh all_enabled example/testapp

# Verify the generated project compiles
cd example/testapp && flutter pub get && flutter analyze
```
